I have also encountered a similar issue. Is there any progress on this problem now?

```
function fn() {
  fn = function () {
    return {};
  };
}

eval('');

function callFn() {
  fn();
}
```

This code will be compiled into the following content：

```
"use strict";
function fn1() {
    fn1 = function fn1() {
        return {};
    };
}
eval("");
function callFn() {
    fn();
}
```

If there is no eval expression, this is as expected. it will be compiled into something like this.

```
"use strict";
function fn() {
    fn = function fn() {
        return {};
    };
}
function callFn() {
    fn();
}
```
